{
	"nodes":[
		{
			"id":"fc792b87aef159aa",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Response to the Great Depression",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-180,
			"y":-20,
			"width":325,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"d3f2c48c3f4108e2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"1. **Protectionism**\nSome countries (Britain, France and the US) => introduced tariffs => to protect their own industries and limit or stop imports. \nTheir trading partners did the same => resulting in overall fall in trade volumes. ",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-520,
			"y":-440,
			"width":376,
			"height":320
		},
		{
			"id":"3cb3694aa231f3f3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"2. **Calling in Loans**\nAs the US economy struggled => US banks called in their loans.\nLed to collapse of Banks and businesses which in turn caused mass unemployment",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":145,
			"y":-440,
			"width":400,
			"height":240
		},
		{
			"id":"a5197a8bfbbd883d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"4. **Radicalism**\nIn some countries => Great Depression helped bring radical regimes to power => most notably the Nazi party in Germany.\nin other states such as italy => the GD caused existing regimes to adopt more extreme and aggressive policies. ",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":145,
			"y":209,
			"width":375,
			"height":391
		},
		{
			"id":"0b8bc6123134ed38",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":220,
			"y":20,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"3df0395415e5e065",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"3. **Rearmament**\nMany countries (Britain, France, Italy and Japan) began the rearmament process to boost industry and create jobs for the unemployed ",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-450,
			"y":240,
			"width":306,
			"height":303
		}
	],
